The syntax error arises because Alloy 6 does not allow multiple top-level quantified expressions (such as some ... | ... and all ... | ...) within a single parenthesized block joined by "and". All previous attempts tried to group or sequence these quantifiers, but Alloy expects the assert body to be a single Boolean formula, not a conjunction of separate quantified expressions. The root cause is that the assertion is structured as a parenthesized block containing two independent quantified formulas joined by "and", which violates Alloy's parsing rules. Furthermore, the use of parentheses here does not convert two quantified statements into a single Boolean expression in Alloy 6. Instead, Alloy requires combining such requirements either by merging the quantifiers, flattening into a single quantifier, or by using an auxiliary predicate to encapsulate the multi-quantifier logic.

