Previous Lessons:
1. Alloy 6 requires Boolean-valued functions to specify their return type as Bool and use a single Boolean formula as the body; curly braces for function bodies require a return value, not a predicate/Boolean formula.
2. Can't use 'if ... then ... else ...' expressions or "if-then-else" in Alloy 6 → Must use 'condition => expr1 else expr2' conditional operator and logical connectives to encode conditional logic.
3. Alloy requires careful bracketing for multiline conditional expressions; failure to enclose such expressions causes syntax errors blocking verification.
4. Alloy 6 requires all function declarations to have an explicit return type; omitting the return type causes a syntax error.
5. Can't use "if-then-else" directly in Alloy 6 facts or predicates → Must use implication (=>) or conditional expressions in let bindings.

